      "extract": "The Einstein equation Gµν = 0, (1) and the incompressible Navier-Stokes equation ˙vi−η∂ 2vi +∂iP +vj∂jvi = 0, (2) have long played central roles in both mathematics and physics. The Einstein equation universally governs the long-distance behavior of essentially any gravitating system, while the incompressible Navier-Stokes equation universally governs the hydrodynamic limit of essentially any ﬂuid. They both display",
      "extractCut": true
